{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And he calls out against you.</b> One might think it is a commandment — Scripture says, ״וְלֹא יִקְרָא״." "<b>And it shall be a sin in you.</b> In any case, even if he does not call out. If so, why is ״וְקָרָא עָלֶיךָ״ stated? I hasten to exact punishment on account of the one who calls out, more than one who does not call out (ibid.)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:10.619842713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}